<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chertsey Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">666–<a href="/years/1537">1537</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chertsey Abbey was a Benedictine abbey at Chertsey in Surrey, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, founded in 666 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eorcenwald">Eorcenwald</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, and endowed by the sub-king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frithuwold">Frithuwold</a>. Sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> in the 9th century, it was refounded in the 10th century and became one of the richest abbeys in England. It was dissolved in 1537 and almost entirely demolished.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chertsey-abbey.jpg" alt="Chertsey Abbey" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johnbod · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stained_glass_in_the_Burrell_CollectionDSCF0487_14.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
